2. Design & Analysis 
• Tie-Break Order: 'price' precedes 'received' (both count 2) because tuple comparison (-2, 'price') < (-2, 'received') 
compares strings lexicographically when counts are equal. 
• O(1) Average Lookup: Python computes hash(key) to jump directly to a slot in an open-addressed hash table, 
making lookup independent of dictionary size. 
• Insertion Order & Views: Since Python 3.7, compact dictionaries preserve insertion order. keys(), values(), and 
items() return dynamic view objects reflecting live dictionary updates without copying data. 
